{"kb/l1/95_CrossEntropyLoss": "SAFE (but reverses the team's P_TASK_TWINS call): plain CE over given logits; 13p/64p's vocab GEMM (>99% of FLOPs) is absent", "authored/moe_expert_ffn_batched/moe_expert_ffn_batched_2": "SAFE (riskier): two per-expert batched GEMMs with GELU (dispatched tokens), not 10p's dense SwiGLU over all experts", "authored/attention_cross/encdec_cross_attention_key_padding": "SAFE: projections 62.5% of FLOPs; key-padding cross-attention core 37.5%", "authored/attention_cross/encdec_cross_attention_padmask": "SAFE: projections 74.5%", "authored/attention_cross/encdec_cross_attention_padmask__m1_splitk": "SAFE: projections 72%", "authored/attention_cross/padded_cross_attention": "SAFE: projections 60%", "kernelbook/Attention_2381": "SAFE: returns the (16,2048,2048) attention weights; P write dominates bytes", "kernelbook/CPAMDec_10410": "SAFE (borderline): attention core 65.6% (<2/3), 256 keys", "kernelbook/GlobalAttentionGeneral_5169": "SAFE: returns the attention map; 128 keys; context projection", "kernelbook/GlobalAttentionGeneral_8369": "SAFE: returns the attention map; 128 keys", "kernelbook/MultiheadAttention_17488": "SAFE: bare SDPA but must also write the (8,4,2048,2048) probability matrix (16x the output bytes); not a flash kernel", "kb/l2/27_Conv3d_HardSwish_GroupNorm_Mean": "SAFE (riskier): 25k chain + HardSwish and a spatial-only final mean; distinct KernelBench L2 problem", "kb/l2/70_Gemm_Sigmoid_Scaling_ResidualAdd": "SAFE (riskier): 30k chain + one sigmoid; distinct KernelBench L2 problem", "kb/l2/73_Conv2d_BatchNorm_Scaling": "SAFE (riskier): 34k minus Mish; distinct KernelBench L2 problem", "authored/attention_alibi/bloom_alibi_padded_attention_block_2": "SAFE: QKV/out projections are 80% of FLOPs; attention core 20%", "authored/attention_alibi/bloom_alibi_padded_attention_block_2__m1_aux": "SAFE: as parent", "authored/attention_gqa_sink/gqa_sink_ring_cache_spec_verify": "SAFE (riskier): ring-buffer modular addressing + window + sinks + 4-token verify", "kernelbook/AR_12699": "SAFE: GEMV (N=1); the team's twin list left KernelBench L1 #4 matvec out", "kernelbook/AR_9990": "SAFE: GEMV (N=1)", "kernelbook/LinearEmbedder_13109": "SAFE (riskier): GEMM+bias with a row-L2-normalise epilogue", "kernelbook/DQN_hot1_17174": "SAFE (riskier): first layer 16384->15 GEMM+bias+ReLU is 99% of FLOPs but N=15 makes it a bandwidth-bound skinny GEMM (GEMV regime)", "kernelbook/GEGLU_11635": "SAFE (riskier): GELU-GLU gate/up only (no down projection, 1/3 of 9p FLOPs) and GELU for SiLU"}
